<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tripoli, Greece</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tripolitsa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a>, known in Ottoman times as Tripolitsa, is a city in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a>. Under Ottoman rule it was the seat of the pasha of the Morea. In September 1821 Greek insurgents under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoros-kolokotronis">Theodoros Kolokotronis</a> captured it after a siege, followed by a massacre of its Muslim and Jewish inhabitants. It was destroyed by Ibrahim Pasha's army in 1828 and later rebuilt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tripoli-greece.jpg" alt="Tripoli, Greece" width="320" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pitichinaccio · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2011_Dimos_Tripolis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
